WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.179 --> 00:00:04.279
The personnel of the SCP Foundation are proud,
highly-trained professionals.

00:00:04.279 --> 00:00:09.270
They are selected from the best of the best
from universities and militaries across the

00:00:09.270 --> 00:00:10.270
world.

00:00:10.270 --> 00:00:15.390
The researchers, agents, and soldiers that
do the daily work of securing, containing,

00:00:15.390 --> 00:00:19.920
and protecting the world from anomalies, take
their duties very seriously.

00:00:19.920 --> 00:00:24.300
When the fate of millions potentially relies
on your daily decision-making, things can

00:00:24.300 --> 00:00:26.840
be a little intense to say the least.

00:00:26.840 --> 00:00:30.570
Kind of makes you want to take back that old
Uber driving gig now doesn’t it?

00:00:30.570 --> 00:00:34.710
But with the massive amounts of personnel
the Foundation hires, it’s inevitable that

00:00:34.710 --> 00:00:37.820
not every employee lives up to this high standard.

00:00:37.820 --> 00:00:41.989
In fact, sometimes they purposefully subvert
the standard.

00:00:41.989 --> 00:00:46.720
Whether it be for personal gain, power, or
something else entirely, the consequences

00:00:46.720 --> 00:00:50.420
of exploiting their position is often disastrous.

00:00:50.420 --> 00:00:56.440
SCP-321 is living - if you can call it that
- evidence of one such incident.

00:00:56.440 --> 00:01:02.570
The file itself is heavily classified - in
fact, it’s been personally redacted by O5-12,

00:01:02.570 --> 00:01:08.110
one of the thirteen mysterious Overseers that
control the day-to-day operations of the Foundation.

00:01:08.110 --> 00:01:11.090
As for why… that will eventually become
clear.

00:01:11.090 --> 00:01:16.101
In fact, it’s so heavily classified and
hidden from main Foundation servers that it

00:01:16.101 --> 00:01:19.630
isn’t even possible to show it here in its
full state.

00:01:19.630 --> 00:01:24.409
But that doesn’t matter, anyway - because
SCP-321 isn’t the kind of thing you can

00:01:24.409 --> 00:01:25.409
read.

00:01:25.409 --> 00:01:29.000
It’s so visceral, you need to see it to
believe it.

00:01:29.000 --> 00:01:31.450
So put on your lab coat and get your clearance
card.

00:01:31.450 --> 00:01:37.130
We’re going down into the bowels of Site-04
to find out just what this strange anomaly

00:01:37.130 --> 00:01:42.210
is that an Overseer is so insistent on hiding
from the world.

00:01:42.210 --> 00:01:45.520
Imagine you’ve been working at the Foundation
for several years.

00:01:45.520 --> 00:01:47.500
You’ve seen all the famous anomalies.

00:01:47.500 --> 00:01:54.400
You’ve taken tissue samples from SCP-682,
you’ve conducted material tests with SCP-914

00:01:54.400 --> 00:01:57.520
and you’ve even interviewed SCP-049.

00:01:57.520 --> 00:02:02.180
All the other researchers have shown you the
ropes but you’ve more than surpassed them.

00:02:02.180 --> 00:02:06.660
Your superiors have taken notice that you
have a good, clean track record with intelligent

00:02:06.660 --> 00:02:08.479
and humanoid anomalies.

00:02:08.479 --> 00:02:13.700
You’ve recently been promoted from Junior
Researcher to a full-fledged Foundation Researcher,

00:02:13.700 --> 00:02:16.230
and your clearance class has gone up.

00:02:16.230 --> 00:02:19.930
You can now access files for most anomalies
in the course of your duties.

00:02:19.930 --> 00:02:23.220
But working at the SCP Foundation isn’t
all fun and games.

00:02:23.220 --> 00:02:26.819
There’s a whole lot of paperwork to fill
out.

00:02:26.819 --> 00:02:32.269
Paperwork for tests, paperwork for new anomalies,
paperwork for every little containment update

00:02:32.269 --> 00:02:37.389
whether it be a dietary change or completely
altering an anomaly’s containment method.

00:02:37.389 --> 00:02:42.999
You spend long, long hours between meetings
or tests in your office at your Foundation-issue

00:02:42.999 --> 00:02:48.859
terminal, poring over SCP files and documents
to print out or put together briefings on.

00:02:48.859 --> 00:02:53.769
During one of these late-night work sessions,
having gone down a rabbit hole into SCPs filed

00:02:53.769 --> 00:02:58.780
under ‘reanimation’ and ‘humanoid’
tags, you encounter a hyperlink to the file

00:02:58.780 --> 00:03:01.219
for SCP-321.

00:03:01.219 --> 00:03:05.400
Mildly intrigued at the memorable number,
you click it - only to be caught off guard

00:03:05.400 --> 00:03:07.849
entirely when your terminal freezes up.

00:03:07.849 --> 00:03:13.290
The screen locks up, and a single message
flashes on the screen: “UNAUTHORIZED ACCESS!

00:03:13.290 --> 00:03:15.540
AUTOMATICALLY SHUTTING DOWN!”.

00:03:15.540 --> 00:03:20.779
The machine reboots itself and seems fine,
but you’re startled by the experience.

00:03:20.779 --> 00:03:25.219
Though obviously it’s not unheard of - sometimes
documents in the Foundation are just locked

00:03:25.219 --> 00:03:27.669
up and people forget to make note of it.

00:03:27.669 --> 00:03:32.280
This SCP-321 must be just another file, nothing
to worry about.

00:03:32.280 --> 00:03:36.719
You know that, but that doesn’t stop you
from sleeping with the lights on in your dormitory

00:03:36.719 --> 00:03:37.719
that night.

00:03:37.719 --> 00:03:42.709
The next morning when you report the incident
to your supervisor she seems disinterested.

00:03:42.709 --> 00:03:47.750
She assures you it was just a minor unauthorized
access hiccup, it happens all the time within

00:03:47.750 --> 00:03:48.750
the database.

00:03:48.750 --> 00:03:53.459
But when she asks you what file it was out
of curiosity and you respond with the number

00:03:53.459 --> 00:03:58.049
SCP-321 - well, her response is… odd.

00:03:58.049 --> 00:04:02.339
She quietly writes something down, muttering
something about “Adam”, and curtly dismisses

00:04:02.339 --> 00:04:03.819
you to get back to work.

00:04:03.819 --> 00:04:10.739
It’s a curious mystery, but it stays a mystery,
and you don’t hear about SCP-321 again for

00:04:10.739 --> 00:04:12.260
a long time.

00:04:12.260 --> 00:04:13.260
It’s years later.

00:04:13.260 --> 00:04:18.709
You’ve participated in hundreds more research
inquiries and thousands of tests and experiments

00:04:18.709 --> 00:04:19.709
since.

00:04:19.709 --> 00:04:24.930
Your skill with anomalies is pretty notable
in Site-04 now, and you stand out in a crowd.

00:04:24.930 --> 00:04:27.659
Your position rises appropriately - congratulations!

00:04:27.659 --> 00:04:30.680
You’ve made Senior Researcher.

00:04:30.680 --> 00:04:34.539
Very few ever get to this position, much less
at your age.

00:04:34.539 --> 00:04:39.550
You supervise research over dozens of anomalies
and over a hundred staff.

00:04:39.550 --> 00:04:42.940
Though you don’t do much testing with your
own hands anymore.

00:04:42.940 --> 00:04:47.629
It’s too risky to send Senior Researchers
in for grunt work, and your role is mostly

00:04:47.629 --> 00:04:50.350
one of oversight and supervising.

00:04:50.350 --> 00:04:54.580
So when you receive an email one late night
on your terminal for containment procedures

00:04:54.580 --> 00:04:58.460
of some anomaly you’ve never heard of, you’re
not too surprised.

00:04:58.460 --> 00:05:02.650
But when you read the subject line, that changes.

00:05:02.650 --> 00:05:04.430
SCP-321.

00:05:04.430 --> 00:05:09.720
The same mysterious anomaly that nearly bricked
your terminal when you were just a researcher.

00:05:09.720 --> 00:05:13.979
You’re now about to find out what was so
secret that it needed to be restricted so

00:05:13.979 --> 00:05:15.169
heavily.

00:05:15.169 --> 00:05:19.759
You click the email, holding your breath and
find Nothing.

00:05:19.759 --> 00:05:25.740
No description of the anomaly, no addendums,
and certainly no images or supplements.

00:05:25.740 --> 00:05:28.229
Just a partially filled out SCP document.

00:05:28.229 --> 00:05:31.889
Item number 3890, object class safe.

00:05:31.889 --> 00:05:36.539
All that’s there is a sparse set of containment
procedures:

00:05:36.539 --> 00:05:40.910
“SCP-321 is to be kept in a regulation containment
chamber.

00:05:40.910 --> 00:05:45.979
SCP-321 has been outfitted with extensive
braces, to make up for weaknesses in bone

00:05:45.979 --> 00:05:48.039
structure and muscle mass.

00:05:48.039 --> 00:05:52.229
Its artificial heart is to be examined once
a month for any damage.

00:05:52.229 --> 00:05:55.349
SCP-321 is to be fed three times daily.

00:05:55.349 --> 00:05:58.699
Solid foods are excluded from its prescribed
diet.

00:05:58.699 --> 00:06:03.999
Three staff members are on temporary SCP-321
assignment at this time.

00:06:03.999 --> 00:06:09.169
SCP-321 is to be given three hours a day of
exercise and physical therapy, with the rest

00:06:09.169 --> 00:06:13.590
of its time not involved in experiments to
be confined to its cell.

00:06:13.590 --> 00:06:19.509
While SCP-321 is incapable of asking for anything,
it has been allowed several stuffed toys.”

00:06:19.509 --> 00:06:22.039
Very, very strange.

00:06:22.039 --> 00:06:27.099
It seems to be some kind of humanoid anomaly,
but it’s not clear whether its sentient

00:06:27.099 --> 00:06:28.099
or not.

00:06:28.099 --> 00:06:33.469
It also seems remarkably fragile - with all
sorts of medical shunts and splints to counteract

00:06:33.469 --> 00:06:37.479
extensive calcium deficiency in the bones
and atrophied muscles.

00:06:37.479 --> 00:06:39.169
And an artificial heart?

00:06:39.169 --> 00:06:44.060
Lots of resources are being spent on keeping
this thing - whatever it is - alive.

00:06:44.060 --> 00:06:49.469
But what kind of a life does it live, not
even being able to eat properly and needing

00:06:49.469 --> 00:06:52.660
constant physical therapy between experiments.

00:06:52.660 --> 00:06:55.990
The stuffed animals thing is even more haunting.

00:06:55.990 --> 00:07:00.370
Stuffed animals are something the Foundation
tends to reserve for child anomalies.

00:07:00.370 --> 00:07:02.699
And why can’t it request anything?

00:07:02.699 --> 00:07:07.300
All you can conclude is that the Foundation
is, for whatever reason, keeping a fragile

00:07:07.300 --> 00:07:13.590
mute child in the maximum security wing of
Site-04 and not letting anyone know about

00:07:13.590 --> 00:07:14.590
it.

00:07:14.590 --> 00:07:19.469
It’s not a pleasant thought, but you know
that these things aren’t done for no reason.

00:07:19.469 --> 00:07:25.560
Whatever this anomaly is, it likely poses
a danger to itself or people around it, and

00:07:25.560 --> 00:07:27.620
needs this level of security.

00:07:27.620 --> 00:07:32.139
You approve the containment procedures, close
your email, and go to sleep.

00:07:32.139 --> 00:07:40.270
And once again, that’s all you hear of SCP-321,
whatever it is, for a very long time.

00:07:40.270 --> 00:07:44.300
Site Director is an incredibly prestigious
position in the Foundation.

00:07:44.300 --> 00:07:50.559
These titans manage massive Foundation installations
and facilities - they’re the executives,

00:07:50.559 --> 00:07:53.400
the big-shots, the decision-makers.

00:07:53.400 --> 00:07:55.270
Where the buck stops.

00:07:55.270 --> 00:07:59.760
Some maintain the researcher roots they came
from and others fall fully into the role of

00:07:59.760 --> 00:08:03.259
power player in the Foundation’s complicated
internal politics.

00:08:03.259 --> 00:08:08.880
Either way, it’s a very high level of power
most people never get anywhere near.

00:08:08.880 --> 00:08:12.509
When you’re made Assistant Site Director,
you know it’s not the real thing and that

00:08:12.509 --> 00:08:14.650
getting up there is still a few years off.

00:08:14.650 --> 00:08:19.419
But that doesn’t stop you from feeling incredibly
proud of how far you’ve come in your career

00:08:19.419 --> 00:08:24.590
at the Foundation, how many breaches you’ve
stopped and lives you’ve saved by keeping

00:08:24.590 --> 00:08:26.790
dangerous anomalies locked up.

00:08:26.790 --> 00:08:31.099
You can access the full database file on nearly
every SCP in the site’s catalogue now.

00:08:31.099 --> 00:08:35.750
It doesn’t take long before you think back
to the strange anomaly that had repeatedly

00:08:35.750 --> 00:08:39.940
cropped up in your career and decide to now
bury the mystery.

00:08:39.940 --> 00:08:46.160
You check in with your credentials and navigate
to the SCP-321 file to see what’s what.

00:08:46.160 --> 00:08:50.570
It’s just your luck that the database file
is completely empty!

00:08:50.570 --> 00:08:55.010
All that’s there are the same containment
procedures you authorized so many years ago

00:08:55.010 --> 00:09:00.620
and a short message from RAISA - that the
SCP-321 file hasn’t been digitized yet and

00:09:00.620 --> 00:09:05.500
that a physical copy is available in SCP-321’s
containment chamber.

00:09:05.500 --> 00:09:09.560
Strange, but at least now you have somewhere
to go.

00:09:09.560 --> 00:09:14.180
SCP-321’s chamber is deep, deep below Site-04.

00:09:14.180 --> 00:09:18.870
It takes you three elevators and security
checkpoints to even get down there.

00:09:18.870 --> 00:09:24.160
This is where the top-secret anomalies are
kept - not necessarily dangerous, but things

00:09:24.160 --> 00:09:27.980
the Foundation would prefer not get out to
even their own employees.

00:09:27.980 --> 00:09:31.620
It’s a dark hallway lined with steel doors.

00:09:31.620 --> 00:09:36.010
You find the right door and scan your card,
and a guard waves you in.

00:09:36.010 --> 00:09:40.690
You’re in an observation room of some kind,
with one large window looking out into an

00:09:40.690 --> 00:09:42.410
adjoining containment chamber.

00:09:42.410 --> 00:09:47.720
There’s computer screens all over the walls,
displaying medical information and data.

00:09:47.720 --> 00:09:53.230
There’s no one else in the room, but something
is lying in the hospital bed in the containment

00:09:53.230 --> 00:09:54.230
chamber.

00:09:54.230 --> 00:09:59.870
There’s a clipboard hanging from the wall,
bearing the designation “SCP-321”.

00:09:59.870 --> 00:10:04.259
You pick it up and carry it with you as you
enter the containment chamber and approach

00:10:04.259 --> 00:10:06.160
the hospital bed.

00:10:06.160 --> 00:10:08.240
SCP-321 lies in the bed.

00:10:08.240 --> 00:10:13.400
It’s a long, distended looking humanoid
- almost 10 feet in length but incredibly

00:10:13.400 --> 00:10:15.020
thin and frail looking.

00:10:15.020 --> 00:10:20.940
It’s hair is thinning and the skin is taut
around its face but you can discern some decidedly

00:10:20.940 --> 00:10:23.060
feminine-looking features.

00:10:23.060 --> 00:10:27.850
Its eyes are closed - the thing is asleep,
and you give it a closer look as you cross-check

00:10:27.850 --> 00:10:30.089
it with its documentation.

00:10:30.089 --> 00:10:35.269
“SCP-321 is a human female, born some time
in the 1800s.

00:10:35.269 --> 00:10:42.040
SCP-321 is currently 3.1 meters tall, and
weighs approximately 110 kilograms.

00:10:42.040 --> 00:10:45.910
Subject is devoid of melanins in hair, eyes,
and skin.”

00:10:45.910 --> 00:10:47.279
Yep, that checks out.

00:10:47.279 --> 00:10:50.130
The anomaly is white as a ghost.

00:10:50.130 --> 00:10:54.759
The document says that it can’t speak and
seems to have trouble with spatial recognition,

00:10:54.759 --> 00:10:58.880
intelligence, and awareness, like a child.

00:10:58.880 --> 00:11:02.990
Then it hits you - this thing must be from
the 19th century.

00:11:02.990 --> 00:11:07.000
The next paragraph is redacted, but the one
after that is fascinating.

00:11:07.000 --> 00:11:10.690
You look at it as you circle SCP-321’s bed.

00:11:10.690 --> 00:11:15.510
It has complex regeneration abilities, and
is capable of healing injuries and wounds

00:11:15.510 --> 00:11:18.370
five times faster than a normal person.

00:11:18.370 --> 00:11:23.880
It ages incredibly slowly - which makes sense,
it should be dead by now if it was born well

00:11:23.880 --> 00:11:25.570
over a century ago.

00:11:25.570 --> 00:11:31.490
It’s noted down that its aging has stopped
entirely but it keeps growing taller and larger

00:11:31.490 --> 00:11:36.509
despite being already over 10 feet tall, well
past the point where it’s heart should’ve

00:11:36.509 --> 00:11:37.509
given out.

00:11:37.509 --> 00:11:39.990
In fact, its heart did give out.

00:11:39.990 --> 00:11:44.360
Somewhere in the 20th century, it became too
tall for its heart to properly circulate blood

00:11:44.360 --> 00:11:45.360
to it.

00:11:45.360 --> 00:11:49.650
This is the same condition that results in
genetic ‘giants’ dying so young.

00:11:49.650 --> 00:11:55.170
But SCP-321 was restrained by the Foundation
to ensure blood kept flowing to its brain,

00:11:55.170 --> 00:12:00.270
though this was a losing battle - its healing
factor was unable to repair tissue damage

00:12:00.270 --> 00:12:03.000
happening constantly and in real time.

00:12:03.000 --> 00:12:07.889
Decay and necrosis began to set in to its
muscles and organs.

00:12:07.889 --> 00:12:09.509
The Foundation stepped in.

00:12:09.509 --> 00:12:14.579
Just after World War 2, a team of researchers
began working to create a sort of artificial

00:12:14.579 --> 00:12:19.370
heart that would allow SCP-321 to keep on
pumping blood.

00:12:19.370 --> 00:12:22.300
Not too unlike the modern pacemaker device,
actually.

00:12:22.300 --> 00:12:27.589
It was finished some years later and an expert-trained
team of Foundation surgeons were tasked with

00:12:27.589 --> 00:12:28.740
implanting it.

00:12:28.740 --> 00:12:34.779
Since they successfully completed the operation,
all of SCP-321’s internal damage has healed

00:12:34.779 --> 00:12:35.779
perfectly.

00:12:35.779 --> 00:12:40.829
More test revealed that its remarkable recuperative
abilities came from an abundance of stem cells

00:12:40.829 --> 00:12:43.430
after exposure to an anomaly after…

00:12:43.430 --> 00:12:44.430
death?

00:12:44.430 --> 00:12:46.579
You look back up at the thing, and back down.

00:12:46.579 --> 00:12:48.420
Is this a practical joke of some kind?

00:12:48.420 --> 00:12:51.529
You’ve seen stranger things than this but
still…

00:12:51.529 --> 00:12:52.740
a zombie?

00:12:52.740 --> 00:12:56.810
But it doesn’t seem to be a zombie, though
it is undead.

00:12:56.810 --> 00:13:03.050
It’s still human, at least apparently - it’s
been taught to eat and play with some toys,

00:13:03.050 --> 00:13:07.510
as well as exercise itself, though it took
researchers years to train it to do so.

00:13:07.510 --> 00:13:12.110
They’ve also figured out that its vocal
chords are intact - but for whatever reason,

00:13:12.110 --> 00:13:16.250
it can’t learn to speak, just crying and
babbling like an infant.

00:13:16.250 --> 00:13:19.360
The remaining two paragraphs are under the
subheader “Origin”.

00:13:19.360 --> 00:13:25.829
But they are again redacted in marker, and
attributed to the Office of O5-12.

00:13:25.829 --> 00:13:30.529
For some reason where this strange undead
woman came from is a highly-guarded secret

00:13:30.529 --> 00:13:33.149
that O5-12 doesn’t want getting out.

00:13:33.149 --> 00:13:35.759
Very, very strange.

00:13:35.759 --> 00:13:39.040
But ultimately this is all you can do, for
now.

00:13:39.040 --> 00:13:42.010
Obviously this thing is eking out a pitiful
existence down here.

00:13:42.010 --> 00:13:44.629
Who knows if its even self-conscious?

00:13:44.629 --> 00:13:46.209
If it can feel pain?

00:13:46.209 --> 00:13:51.160
It’s unfortunate and depressing but after
so many years in the upper echelons of the

00:13:51.160 --> 00:13:56.540
Foundation’s research staff, you’ve seen
some terrible, terrible things.

00:13:56.540 --> 00:13:59.510
This is very sad, but what can you do?

00:13:59.510 --> 00:14:04.430
The heart monitor in the room continues beeping
as you hang up the clipboard in the observation

00:14:04.430 --> 00:14:06.440
room and take your leave.

00:14:06.440 --> 00:14:10.649
It really doesn’t surprise anyone when you
eventually become Site Director just a few

00:14:10.649 --> 00:14:11.829
short years later.

00:14:11.829 --> 00:14:16.029
You’re given a warm welcome into the new
job, but there’s really no time to relax

00:14:16.029 --> 00:14:17.029
at all.

00:14:17.029 --> 00:14:19.590
Running a Foundation site is busy work.

00:14:19.590 --> 00:14:23.759
Lots of meetings and important briefings to
be had - which is how you find yourself heading

00:14:23.759 --> 00:14:26.910
to a meeting in the site with O5-12.

00:14:26.910 --> 00:14:32.140
One of the strange, mysterious O5s that rule
the Foundation with an iron fist, subject

00:14:32.140 --> 00:14:36.500
to no one but the Ethics Committee - what
could he possibly want with you?

00:14:36.500 --> 00:14:42.250
Not to mention the fact that this meeting
is in none other than SCP-321’s containment

00:14:42.250 --> 00:14:43.250
chamber.

00:14:43.250 --> 00:14:45.050
When you arrive, you catch a glance of him.

00:14:45.050 --> 00:14:49.680
He’s an incredibly old-looking man, healthy
but leaning on a cane.

00:14:49.680 --> 00:14:53.390
You make small talk for a moment before he
starts talking about the anomaly lying in

00:14:53.390 --> 00:14:55.769
the hospital bed in front of you two.

00:14:55.769 --> 00:15:01.020
He explains that over a century ago, a Foundation
Junior Researcher named Adam had developed

00:15:01.020 --> 00:15:05.230
a relationship with one of his colleagues,
a doctor named Evelyn.

00:15:05.230 --> 00:15:09.370
The rules regarding relationships between
coworkers were much looser then, and they

00:15:09.370 --> 00:15:11.130
married each other not long after.

00:15:11.130 --> 00:15:16.019
They even had a child together - at least,
they were going to.

00:15:16.019 --> 00:15:19.750
Unfortunately, tragedy struck not long after
Evelyn became pregnant.

00:15:19.750 --> 00:15:23.360
The infant didn’t make it, and was stillborn.

00:15:23.360 --> 00:15:27.569
But Adam, unwilling to give up, began to conduct
experiments on the corpse.

00:15:27.569 --> 00:15:34.550
Using SCP-590, another one of Adam's anomalous
children named TJ, and a number of other SCPs,

00:15:34.550 --> 00:15:39.209
he somehow managed to bring what remained
of his daughter back to life.

00:15:39.209 --> 00:15:44.519
Well, to something resembling life - but the
Foundation quickly intervened when they discovered

00:15:44.519 --> 00:15:46.480
what Adam had created.

00:15:46.480 --> 00:15:50.800
They collected the creature and began to examine
and experiment on her, which is when they

00:15:50.800 --> 00:15:55.129
discovered her amazing ability to heal from
practically any wound.

00:15:55.129 --> 00:16:01.040
She was quickly classified SCP-321 and placed
into containment for experimentation.

00:16:01.040 --> 00:16:05.110
But Adam was still a Junior Researcher at
the Foundation, and he knew his daughter was

00:16:05.110 --> 00:16:07.980
undergoing cruel and invasive experimentation.

00:16:07.980 --> 00:16:13.300
He couldn’t live with the guilt - first
of losing his wife, then his daughter.

00:16:13.300 --> 00:16:19.350
He made several formal requests for SCP-321
to be removed from SCP status on the basis

00:16:19.350 --> 00:16:21.410
that it was unnecessary.

00:16:21.410 --> 00:16:24.000
All were denied by the O5 Council.

00:16:24.000 --> 00:16:28.069
Years later, Adam had been promoted to Personnel
Director at Site-04.

00:16:28.069 --> 00:16:34.689
He again requested SCP-321 be released from
containment, and was again given a firm no.

00:16:34.689 --> 00:16:37.560
But a father’s love never goes away.

00:16:37.560 --> 00:16:41.890
As he kept being promoted, he kept requesting
his daughter be freed into his custody.

00:16:41.890 --> 00:16:47.329
When he became Site Director of Site-04, just
as you had joined the Foundation, he made

00:16:47.329 --> 00:16:52.600
a statement declaring that there was nothing
more the Foundation had to learn from SCP-321

00:16:52.600 --> 00:16:54.339
and that it should be released.

00:16:54.339 --> 00:16:56.790
But again, nothing but denial.

00:16:56.790 --> 00:17:04.020
And when he was promoted to O5-12, he ordered
that SCP-321 be released and returned to her

00:17:04.020 --> 00:17:05.020
family.

00:17:05.020 --> 00:17:11.010
That’s right - O5-12, the old man standing
beside you, is the same man that fathered

00:17:11.010 --> 00:17:15.030
and created SCP-321 so many years ago.

00:17:15.030 --> 00:17:17.190
And that’s not all, either.

00:17:17.190 --> 00:17:23.720
His name is Adam Bright - father of notorious
researcher Doctor Jack Bright, otherwise known

00:17:23.720 --> 00:17:26.470
as SCP-963.

00:17:26.470 --> 00:17:31.670
The Bright family’s history is intertwined
with that of the SCP Foundation, but despite

00:17:31.670 --> 00:17:36.650
all their power, they cannot get one of their
own released from the Foundation’s cells.

00:17:36.650 --> 00:17:41.260
When O5-12 made the decree, O5-1 addressed
him personally.

00:17:41.260 --> 00:17:46.530
He was told that SCP-321 was not his daughter,
if she ever had been.

00:17:46.530 --> 00:17:51.680
And that if he requested her release again,
he would be dismissed from the O5 Council.

00:17:51.680 --> 00:17:56.580
Since then, all he has been able to do is
visit his little girl deep beneath Site-04

00:17:56.580 --> 00:17:59.430
and protect her from further experimentation.

00:17:59.430 --> 00:18:04.510
He explains that he hides and classifies her
existence so heavily to make sure no one tries

00:18:04.510 --> 00:18:08.020
to perform more tests and take advantage of
her healing factor.

00:18:08.020 --> 00:18:12.850
That’s why you were unable to access or
even figure out what the anomaly was for so

00:18:12.850 --> 00:18:14.150
many years.

00:18:14.150 --> 00:18:18.020
All the two of you can do is stand next to
the hospital bed.

00:18:18.020 --> 00:18:23.830
The history of the SCP Foundation is a long
and twisted one, especially considering the

00:18:23.830 --> 00:18:27.460
complex web of relationship between its employees.

00:18:27.460 --> 00:18:32.950
The extensive Bright family, headed by famous
Jack Bright but containing many of his relatives,

00:18:32.950 --> 00:18:34.870
winds throughout the Foundation.

00:18:34.870 --> 00:18:39.760
When one of its members abuses their position,
you’ve seen how terrible the results can

00:18:39.760 --> 00:18:40.760
be.

00:18:40.760 --> 00:18:46.960
As for SCP-321, some anomalies tragically
can’t be saved, and there’s little the

00:18:46.960 --> 00:18:49.050
Foundation can do about that.

00:18:49.050 --> 00:18:53.050
Now go check out “SCP Immortal Dr. Bright
Explained” and “DR.

00:18:53.050 --> 00:18:59.890
BRIGHT FOR PRESIDENT SCP-4444 - Bush v. Gore”
for more on the fascinating intricacies of

00:18:59.890 --> 00:19:01.850
the infamous Dr. Jack Bright!

